<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.Africa mohair prices fall at first winter sale.</title>
<headline>S.Africa mohair prices fall at first winter sale.</headline>
<dateline>PORT ELIZABETH 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African mohair prices were lower at the first winter sale from the last summer sale, figures released by the Mohair Board showed. 98 percent was sold.</p>
<p>Approximate prices in South African cents a kg:</p>
<p>Adults	  long	 2600-2654	  (2622-3502)</p>
<p>		  medium     2450-2610	  (2400-2630)</p>
<p>		  short	2432-2520	  (2202-2500)</p>
<p>Young Goats   long	 2630-2880	  (2650-3460)</p>
<p>		  medium     2480-2572	  (2500-2610)</p>
<p>		  short	2450-2500	  (2302-2500)</p>
<p>Fine Kids     long	 3500-5702	  (3100-10050)</p>
<p>		  medium     3052-3700	  (3500-5000)</p>
<p>		  short	3210-3652	  (2700-3500)</p>
<p>The second winter sale of the season is scheduled for September 17, 1996.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
